@page "/help/keyboard"
@attribute [AllowAnonymous]

@* Pure static content: no interactivity, so this stays static SSR (no @rendermode) and renders
   instantly for the `?` shortcut, which opens it in a new tab from anywhere in the app. *@

<PageTitle>Keyboard Shortcuts - Blocwerk</PageTitle>

<div class="keyshort-page">
    <div class="page-header">
        <a href="/" class="back-link">&larr; Home</a>
        <h1>Keyboard Shortcuts</h1>
        <p class="description">
            These are desktop shortcuts &mdash; they need a physical keyboard. While you are typing in a
            text field, shortcuts never fire, so you can name a hold &ldquo;amber&rdquo; without triggering
            the Add, Move, Border and Paint tools. <kbd>Enter</kbd> and <kbd>Space</kbd> also stay with a
            button, link or label that currently has focus, so tabbing to a button and pressing it still
            does exactly what the button says &mdash; even where the page lists another action for
            <kbd>Enter</kbd>.
        </p>
        <p class="description">
            Some surfaces take the keyboard over completely: while a review stepper, an image lightbox or
            a modal dialog is on screen, the shared shortcuts below (including the wall carousel arrows)
            are all inactive and only that surface's own keys apply.
        </p>
    </div>

    <section class="keyshort-section">
        <h2>Kiosk tablets</h2>
        <p class="keyshort-note">
            On a wall-mounted kiosk tablet, keyboard shortcuts are <strong>off by default</strong> and
            none of the keys below do anything. A kiosk is a shared, unattended device, so a keyboard
            plugged into it could otherwise drive the editing shortcuts &mdash; including
            <kbd>d</kbd>, which deletes a hold.
        </p>
        <p class="keyshort-note">
            A wall admin can turn them on for one wall at a time, from their own device, under that
            wall's <strong>Kiosk Registration</strong> settings.
        </p>
    </section>

    @* One <dl> per surface, one <div class="keyshort-row"> per binding: adding or editing a
       binding later means touching exactly one markup block. *@

    <section class="keyshort-section">
        <h2>Global</h2>
        <p class="keyshort-note">Handled in JavaScript, so it works on every page, including pages with no interactivity.</p>
        <dl class="keyshort-list">
            <div class="keyshort-row">
                <dt><kbd>?</kbd></dt>
                <dd>
                    Open this keyboard shortcuts page <strong>in a new tab</strong>, so looking a key up
                    never leaves the page you are on or throws away staged edits
                </dd>
            </div>
        </dl>
    </section>

    <section class="keyshort-section">
        <h2>Wall page</h2>
        <p class="keyshort-note">Paging through the wall carousel. Disabled while the carousel is locked for editing.</p>
        <dl class="keyshort-list">
            <div class="keyshort-row">
                <dt><kbd>&larr;</kbd></dt>
                <dd>Previous pane</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="keyshort-row">
                <dt><kbd>&rarr;</kbd></dt>
                <dd>Next pane</dd>
            </div>
        </dl>
        <p class="keyshort-note">
            The arrows also stand down whenever a review stepper, an image lightbox or a modal dialog is
            open. In the gallery lightbox that means <kbd>&larr;</kbd>/<kbd>&rarr;</kbd> page through the
            images (and <kbd>Esc</kbd> closes it) instead of moving the carousel behind it.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="keyshort-section">
        <h2>Wall editor</h2>
        <p class="keyshort-note">
            The editor only claims these keys while you have edit rights on the wall and the editor is in
            edit mode. Each key repeats the gate of the button it mirrors, so a key whose tool is not on
            the toolbar in this configuration simply does nothing.
        </p>

        <h3>Tools</h3>
        <dl class="keyshort-list">
            <div class="keyshort-row">
                <dt><kbd>a</kbd></dt>
                <dd>Add hold</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="keyshort-row">
                <dt><kbd>m</kbd></dt>
                <dd>Select / move</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="keyshort-row">
                <dt><kbd>s</kbd></dt>
                <dd>Shape</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="keyshort-row">
                <dt><kbd>p</kbd></dt>
                <dd>Paint</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="keyshort-row">
                <dt><kbd>n</kbd></dt>
                <dd>Name</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="keyshort-row">
                <dt><kbd>d</kbd></dt>
                <dd>Delete</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="keyshort-row">
                <dt><kbd>b</kbd></dt>
                <dd>Border (only where the wall border/shape may be edited)</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="keyshort-row">
                <dt><kbd>t</kbd></dt>
                <dd>Tilt (shape tilt)</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="keyshort-row">
                <dt><kbd>u</kbd></dt>
                <dd>Hold usage (only where the page offers the usage view)</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="keyshort-row">
                <dt><kbd>g</kbd></dt>
                <dd>Merge (staged wall updates only, and not during manual alignment)</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="keyshort-row">
                <dt><kbd>k</kbd></dt>
                <dd>Make actual (outside a staged wall update)</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="keyshort-row">
                <dt><kbd>j</kbd></dt>
                <dd>Join duplicate virtual holds — keep one, absorb the other (outside a staged wall update)</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="keyshort-row">
                <dt><kbd>c</kbd></dt>
                <dd>Mark unchanged</dd>
            </div>
        </dl>

        <h3>View and actions</h3>
        <dl class="keyshort-list">
            <div class="keyshort-row">
                <dt><kbd>l</kbd></dt>
                <dd>Toggle hold labels</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="keyshort-row">
                <dt><kbd>o</kbd></dt>
                <dd>Toggle border / segment outlines</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="keyshort-row">
                <dt><kbd>r</kbd></dt>
                <dd>Re-detect holds (where re-detection is offered, and not while one is running)</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="keyshort-row">
                <dt><kbd>1</kbd>&ndash;<kbd>9</kbd></dt>
                <dd>Pick paint colour N from the palette &mdash; <strong>Paint tool only</strong></dd>
            </div>
            <div class="keyshort-row">
                <dt><kbd>[</kbd> <kbd>]</kbd></dt>
                <dd>Previous / next paint colour (wraps around) &mdash; <strong>Paint tool only</strong></dd>
            </div>
            <div class="keyshort-row">
                <dt><kbd>+</kbd> <kbd>-</kbd></dt>
                <dd>Zoom in / out</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="keyshort-row">
                <dt><kbd>0</kbd></dt>
                <dd>Reset zoom</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="keyshort-row">
                <dt><kbd>Ctrl</kbd> <span class="keyshort-plus">+</span> <kbd>S</kbd></dt>
                <dd>
                    Save changes (<kbd>Cmd</kbd> <span class="keyshort-plus">+</span> <kbd>S</kbd> on
                    macOS) &mdash; claimed only while there is actually something to save, and never
                    during a manual alignment. With nothing staged the browser's own Save is left alone.
                </dd>
            </div>
            <div class="keyshort-row">
                <dt><kbd>Esc</kbd></dt>
                <dd>
                    Cancel the active sub-mode and nothing else: naming, a pending merge, a pending
                    &ldquo;make actual&rdquo;, a pending &ldquo;mark unchanged&rdquo; or a shape tilt, in
                    that order. With no sub-mode pending the editor does not claim <kbd>Esc</kbd> at all.
                </dd>
            </div>
        </dl>
        <p class="keyshort-note">
            <kbd>Esc</kbd> never discards your unsaved changes. Discarding is a deliberate click on the
            labelled button, because a stray keystroke must not throw away staged hold edits.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="keyshort-section">
        <h2>Wall update wizard</h2>
        <p class="keyshort-note">The wizard declares a different set of keys on each step.</p>
        <dl class="keyshort-list">
            <div class="keyshort-row">
                <dt><kbd>Enter</kbd></dt>
                <dd>
                    The primary button of the current step: <em>Resume update</em> on the resume prompt,
                    <em>Start update</em> on the upload step, <em>Continue</em> on the detected-holds step,
                    <em>Continue to overlaps</em> on the carry-over step, <em>Continue</em> on the touch-up
                    step, <em>Apply update</em> on the confirm step, and <em>Done</em> on the final step.
                    It respects the button's own disabled state, so a premature <kbd>Enter</kbd> does
                    nothing. If you have tabbed or clicked onto some other button, that button keeps
                    <kbd>Enter</kbd> and is what gets pressed.
                </dd>
            </div>
            <div class="keyshort-row">
                <dt><kbd>s</kbd></dt>
                <dd>
                    Skip touch-up &mdash; on the detected-holds and touch-up steps only. On the
                    detected-holds step skipping and continuing are the same action.
                </dd>
            </div>
            <div class="keyshort-row">
                <dt><kbd>a</kbd></dt>
                <dd>Toggle &ldquo;+ Add hold&rdquo; &mdash; on the detected-holds, touch-up and carry-over steps</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="keyshort-row">
                <dt><kbd>x</kbd></dt>
                <dd>Remove the selected hold &mdash; same three steps; does nothing when nothing is selected</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="keyshort-row">
                <dt><kbd>Esc</kbd></dt>
                <dd>
                    Close the flow &mdash; only on the resume prompt (<em>Not now</em>), the upload step
                    (<em>Cancel</em>) and the final step (<em>Done</em>)
                </dd>
            </div>
        </dl>
        <p class="keyshort-note">
            <kbd>Esc</kbd> never discards a staged update. It is bound only where closing throws nothing
            away, and is deliberately unbound on the detected-holds, carry-over, neighbour-overlap,
            touch-up and confirm steps, because discarding is irreversible and would go unconfirmed.
            The neighbour-overlap step declares no wizard keys at all &mdash; it is driven entirely by the
            overlap stepper below. The carry-over step also goes quiet while one of its review sub-views
            is open.
        </p>

        <h3>Review steppers</h3>
        <p class="keyshort-note">
            Used while reviewing matched or carried-over holds. While a stepper is on screen it owns the
            keyboard: every shortcut above &mdash; the wizard's own keys and the wall carousel arrows
            included &mdash; is inactive, and only the keys below apply.
        </p>
        <p class="keyshort-note">
            They are the stepper's own keys, so they go to whatever has focus. The stepper takes focus
            itself when it opens and again after every decision, so you can normally just start typing;
            if you clicked something else in between, click the stepper once to hand focus back.
        </p>
        <dl class="keyshort-list">
            <div class="keyshort-row">
                <dt><kbd>Enter</kbd></dt>
                <dd>Confirm the match / accept the carried hold (keep, for new holds)</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="keyshort-row">
                <dt><kbd>c</kbd></dt>
                <dd>Confirm match (neighbour overlaps) / toggle &ldquo;changed&rdquo; (carry-over, except the new-hold list)</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="keyshort-row">
                <dt><kbd>d</kbd></dt>
                <dd>Discard match &mdash; neighbour-overlap stepper only</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="keyshort-row">
                <dt><kbd>m</kbd></dt>
                <dd>Mark hold as moved &mdash; neighbour-overlap stepper only</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="keyshort-row">
                <dt><kbd>x</kbd> <span class="keyshort-plus">or</span> <kbd>Del</kbd></dt>
                <dd>
                    Remove the hold / discard the new hold. <kbd>Del</kbd> works here only &mdash; outside
                    a stepper it is not bound at all, and the wizard's own remove key is <kbd>x</kbd>.
                </dd>
            </div>
            <div class="keyshort-row">
                <dt><kbd>&larr;</kbd> <kbd>&rarr;</kbd></dt>
                <dd>Previous / next item</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="keyshort-row">
                <dt><kbd>Esc</kbd></dt>
                <dd>Cancel the current sub-mode (manual pairing, &ldquo;moved&rdquo; pick, interactive pick)</dd>
            </div>
        </dl>
        <p class="keyshort-note">
            While a sub-mode is open the stepper only listens for <kbd>Enter</kbd> (confirm the pick, and
            <kbd>c</kbd> does the same in the &ldquo;moved&rdquo; pick) and <kbd>Esc</kbd> (cancel it).
        </p>
    </section>
</div>
